{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794478931,"nonce":"q6xASkxKbCftxRLNNzHOylqmgBY=","title":"The vector paint of the nested motion scene places its label about 0.1 px left of where every later frame does","message":"Found with the node table harness (crates/blinc_recorder/tests/animation_paths.rs, scene \"motion nested\", labelled).\n\nAn outer motion container translates in x, an inner one scales and turns, and the inner one holds the label. The reference is a full paint of every frame with no promotion (Path::Vector). From step 1 on, the node table (rows only) matches it exactly. At step 0 the label differs by 302 px, channel 32, and nothing else in the frame does.\n\nMeasured with the label's ink centroid (label frame against the same frame without the label): vector paint (160.71, 121.08), table (161.00, 120.94). The pixel rows show the vector label about 0.1 to 0.2 px left of the table's, which is the outer binding's translate at that step (0.2177 px). At step 1 (translate 0.956 px) both agree to the pixel, so the reference places the label correctly there.\n\nNot found. It is not a value threshold: MotionBindings::get_transform cuts at 0.001, in_motion_subtree is structural, and motion text is not pixel snapped (only static text is, in frame_text). The card and its shadow at step 0 match, so it is only the text. The labelled translate, scale and rotate scenes do not show it. It may be the spring's first tick being read at different moments by the painter and the text collector, or a difference in how an ancestor binding's translate reaches a descendant's text in the collector (new_offset in element_collection).\n\nThe harness holds the scene to the vector paint from step 1 (FROM_SECOND_FRAME). Decide which frame is right before taking that off.","files":null}]}